          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/a174dd4017cf97f283b1848bb31998bfa28465e9"
        }
      ],
      "message": "node, qt: don't write settings.json when dynamic settings are disabled\n\nArgsManager::WriteSettingsFile throws when dynamic settings are disabled\nwith -nosettings, and three call sites in NodeImpl call it unguarded, so\nbitcoin-qt -nosettings aborts on -resetguisettings and on the legacy GUI\nsettings migration. The migration case comes back on every start,\nbecause the abort happens before the legacy key is removed.\n\nGuard the writes, and skip the migration when there is nowhere to\nmigrate to, so legacy Qt settings are left in place rather than silently\ndropped.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "jeanpablo",
        "email": "jpnmoreira15@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-09-06T21:30:26Z"
      },
      "author": {
